  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable urban integration of displacement-affected communities in sub- Saharan African cities: action in the Sudan &#x2013; phase IISustainable urban integration of displacement-affected communities in sub- Saharan African cities: action in the Sudan &#x2013; phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Based on the identified needs and priorities, IOM proposes to implement the intervention Sustainable Urban Integration of Displacement-Affected Communities (SUIDAC) in Sub-Saharan African Cities Action in Sudan (Phase II). For Phase II, IOM considers the potential areas of intervention of the two SUIDAC objectives - listed below - and applies a community-based planning (CBP) approach to identify priorities. Objective 1: Improved self-reliance and social cohesion of DACs (women and men) in the targeted urban and peri-urban areas of Sudan. Objective 2: Strengthened readiness and effectiveness of local city administrations, national governments and regional bodies to respond to the needs of DACs in the urban areas.</narrative>
  </description>
